head"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வேந்து","parts":[{"text":"வேந்து","lemma":"vēntu","gloss":"king"}],"gloss":"king"},{"surface":"உடன்று","parts":[{"text":"உடன்று","lemma":"uṭaṉṟu","gloss":"having angered"}],"gloss":"having angered"},{"surface":"எறிந்த","parts":[{"text":"எறிந்த","lemma":"eṟiṉta","gloss":"thrown"}],"gloss":"thrown"},{"surface":"வேலே","parts":[{"text":"வேலே","lemma":"vēl","gloss":"spear"}],"gloss":"spear indeed"},{"surface":"என்னை","parts":[{"text":"என்னை","lemma":"eṉṉai","gloss":"my lord"}],"gloss":"my lord"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சார்ந்தார்","parts":[{"text":"சார்ந்தார்","lemma":"sārntār","gloss":"dependents"}],"gloss":"dependents"},{"surface":"அகலம்","parts":[{"text":"அகலம்","lemma":"akalam","gloss":"chest"}],"gloss":"chest"},{"surface":"உளம்கழிந்தன்றே","parts":[{"text":"உளம்கழிந்தன்றே","lemma":"uḷamkaḻiṉtaṉṟē","gloss":"indeed went through"}],"gloss":"indeed went through"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உளங்கழி","parts":[{"text":"உளங்கழி","lemma":"uḷamkaḻi","gloss":"heart-piercing"}],"gloss":"heart-piercing"},{"surface":"சுடர்ப்படை","parts":[{"text":"சுடர்ப்படை","lemma":"cuṭarppaṭai","gloss":"bright weapon"}],"gloss":"bright weapon"},{"surface":"ஏந்தி","parts":[{"text":"ஏந்தி","lemma":"ēnti","gloss":"raising"}],"gloss":"raising"},{"surface":"நம்","parts":[{"text":"நம்","lemma":"nam","gloss":"our"}],"gloss":"our"},{"surface":"பெருவிறல்","parts":[{"text":"பெருவிறல்","lemma":"peruviṟal","gloss":"great hero"}],"gloss":"great hero"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஓச்சினன்","parts":[{"text":"ஓச்சினன்","lemma":"ōcciṉaṉ","gloss":"brandished"}],"gloss":"brandished"},{"surface":"துரந்த","parts":[{"text":"துரந்த","lemma":"turanta","gloss":"drove"}],"gloss":"drove"},{"surface":"காலை","parts":[{"text":"காலை","lemma":"kālai","gloss":"time"}],"gloss":"at that time"},{"surface":"மற்று","parts":[{"text":"மற்று","lemma":"maṟṟu","gloss":"then"}],"gloss":"then"},{"surface":"அவன்","parts":[{"text":"அவன்","lemma":"avaṉ","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"he"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புன்தலை","parts":[{"text":"புன்தலை","lemma":"puṉtalai","gloss":"small head"}],"gloss":"small head"},{"surface":"மடப்பிடி","parts":[{"text":"மடப்பிடி","lemma":"maṭappiṭi","gloss":"gentle female elephant"}],"gloss":"gentle female elephant"},{"surface":"நாண","parts":[{"text":"நாண","lemma":"nāṇa","gloss":"to feel ashamed"}],"gloss":"to feel ashamed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குஞ்சரம்","parts":[{"text":"குஞ்சரம்","lemma":"kuñcaram","gloss":"male elephant"}],"gloss":"male elephants"},{"surface":"எல்லாம்","parts":[{"text":"எல்லாம்","lemma":"ellām","gloss":"all"}],"gloss":"all"},{"surface":"புறக்கொடுத்தனவே","parts":[{"text":"புறக்கொடுத்தனவே","lemma":"puṟakkoṭuttaṉavē","gloss":"turned their backs"}],"gloss":"turned their backs"}]}],"literal":"Like poured gold, tight-twisted string's / lightning-like green bee-voiced small lute, / goodness filled, pleasing bard! / Small village king's small-leaved spear / king-ridden elephant's raised forehead-it-is. / King-angered thrown spear indeed, my lord's / dependents' chest, went through indeed. / Heart-piercing bright weapon raising, our great hero / brandished and drove, at that time, his / small-headed gentle female elephant to feel ashamed, / male elephants all turned their backs.","translation":"O bard of great goodness and pleasing songs, who plays the small lute with strings tightly twisted like poured gold, sounding like the hum of green bees and shining like lightning! The small-leaved spear of the lord of our small village is now lodged in the raised forehead of the elephant ridden by the enemy king. The spear thrown by the angry enemy king went right through the chests of those who sought refuge in my lord. When our great hero raised his heart-piercing bright weapon, brandished it, and drove it forward, all the enemy's male elephants turned their backs and fled in shame, as if they were gentle female elephants with small heads.","modern":"உருக்கிய பொன்னைப் போன்ற முறுக்கேறிய நரம்புகளையும், மின்னல் போன்ற பச்சைப் பொன்வண்டின் குரலையும் கொண்ட சிறிய யாழை மீட்டும், நற்பண்புகள் நிறைந்த, விருப்பத்தக்க பாணனே! எமது சிற்றூர் மன்னனின் சிறிய இலை வடிவிலான வேல், பகை வேந்தன் ஏறி வந்த யானையின் உயர்ந்த நெற்றியில் பாய்ந்து நிற்கிறது. பகை வேந்தன் சினந்து எறிந்த வேலோ, என் தலைவனைச் சார்ந்திருந்தோரின் மார்பை ஊடுருவிச் சென்றது. நெஞ்சைப் பிளக்கும் ஒளிரும் படையை ஏந்தி, நம் பெரும் வீரன் அதனை ஓங்கிச் செலுத்தியபோது, பகைவரின் ஆண் யானைகள் அனைத்தும், சிறிய தலையையுடைய பெண் யானைகள் நாணமடையும்படி, அவனுக்குப் முதுகு காட்டி ஓடின.","explanation":"The poet Kovur Kizhar addresses a bard (paṇan) who plays a small lute, praising his musical skill and the beauty of his instrument. He describes the fierce battle fought by the chieftain of a small village against a powerful king. The chieftain's spear is lodged in the forehead of the enemy king's war elephant, showing his immense courage. Meanwhile, the enemy's spear has pierced through the chests of the chieftain's loyal followers who stood as a shield for him. When the chieftain raised his bright weapon and charged, the enemy's mighty male elephants fled in retreat, feeling as ashamed as gentle female elephants. This poem belongs to the Vagai thinai and the theme of Mudin Mullai, celebrating the ancestral bravery and martial pride of a warrior clan.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}